# Local environments and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# The real tenant, app and operator identifiers the public docs use
# placeholders for. Not secrets — a tenant id and an app id authorise nothing —
# but together they name a real tenant, a real registration and a real
# privileged account, which is reconnaissance rather than a credential.
LOCAL.md

# The project's working notes: handover, backlog, roadmap, security review
# working documents, and the archived hosted audit trail (which carries the
# real tenant identifiers). A standalone git repository of its own, committed
# locally and never pushed — the public repository is the product, this is the
# project.
local/

# Never commit anything that could carry tenant state or credentials.
# Backstops, not the primary control — the design has no secret to leak.
.env
.env.*
local_settings.json
config.json
*.pem
*.pfx
*.jsonl

# Audit output, if someone points DSAR_AUDIT_DIR inside the working tree.
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: a bare `audit/` matches a directory
# of that name at *any* depth, which silently excluded `src/dsar/audit/` — the
# package Phase 3 lives in. An ignore rule that hides your own source is worse
# than the accident it was written to prevent.
/audit/
